Description: Simple parental controls for Linux desktops
 Tuxsitter limits screen time per day (school days, weekend, holidays),
 restricts usage to allowed hours, lets parents grant extra time with a PIN
 and filters the internet for children's accounts only. Your own accounts
 stay untouched.
 .
 The per-account DNS filter uses a family DNS provider of your choice
 (OpenDNS FamilyShield by default, CleanBrowsing, Cloudflare for Families,
 AdGuard Family, your own NextDNS profile or a custom server such as a
 Pi-hole), enforces SafeSearch and YouTube Restricted Mode and blocks the
 usual workarounds.
 .
 Made for Linux Mint (Cinnamon); works on other Ubuntu/Debian based desktops.
